Backport of nanoid@3.3.12 fix for CVE-2026-73086 (commit 821dfed).

Integer overflow in nanoid(size): size |= 0 wraps values >= 2^31 to negative,
corrupting the process-wide CSPRNG pool in fillPool(). Guard rejects bytes < 0
or > 1024 before pool state is touched. Patches both index.js and index.cjs.

--- a/index.js
+++ b/index.js
@@ -5,4 +5,5 @@
 let fillPool = bytes => {
+  if (bytes < 0 || bytes > 1024) throw new RangeError('Wrong ID size')
   if (!pool || pool.length < bytes) {
     pool = Buffer.allocUnsafe(bytes * POOL_SIZE_MULTIPLIER)
     crypto.randomFillSync(pool)
